    "3Jn"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The elder unto the wellbeloved Gaius, whom I love in the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For I rejoiced greatly, when the brethren came and testified of the truth that is in thee, even as thou walkest in the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I have no greater joy than to hear that my children walk in truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Beloved, thou doest faithfully whatsoever thou doest to the brethren, and to strangers;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Which have borne witness of thy charity before the church: whom if thou bring forward on their journey after a godly sort, thou shalt do well:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Because that for his name’s sake they went forth, taking nothing of the Gentiles.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "We therefore ought to receive such, that we might be fellowhelpers to the truth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "I wrote unto the church: but Diotrephes, who loveth to have the preeminence among them, receiveth us not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Wherefore, if I come, I will remember his deeds which he doeth, prating against us with malicious words: and not content therewith, neither doth he himself receive the brethren, and forbiddeth them that would, and casteth them out of the church.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Beloved, follow not that which is evil, but that which is good. He that doeth good is of God: but he that doeth evil hath not seen God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Demetrius hath good report of all men, and of the truth itself: yea, and we also bear record; and ye know that our record is true.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "I had many things to write, but I will not with ink and pen write unto thee:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:3-john:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "But I trust I shall shortly see thee, and we shall speak face to face. Peace be to thee. Our friends salute thee. Greet the friends by name.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "3 John 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:3-john:1:14"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
